Add per-item group gating to [PAGE FILE, e.g. lp_xxx.html]. Edit the file in place and don't touch any other file.

## Goal
Hide an item (link, tile, card, row) from anyone who isn't a member of the Launchpad group set on that item. Gating is display-only. Items with no group set behave exactly as before.

## Inputs (fill in)
- Page file: [FILE]
- Where the items come from: [hardcoded JS array / form query via INDICATORS / Smarty-rendered HTML]
- Group field: indicator [ID] on form [form_xxxxx] at [site path]. It holds ONE numeric Launchpad group ID per item. Empty means everyone.
- Sysadmin (group 1) bypass: [yes / no]
- Non-member behavior: hide the item entirely (default)
- Outer page gate: [keep as is / describe]

## Implementation
1. **Viewer's groups.** Inside the branch of the page that real users see, add a hidden element that carries the viewer's groups:
```html
   <div
     id="viewerGroups"
     hidden
     data-groups="<!--{foreach $empMembership['groupID'] as $gid => $member}--><!--{$gid}-->,<!--{/foreach}-->"
   ></div>
```
   This Smarty setup leaves literal `<!--` and `-->` around output values, so read only the digits.
2. **Parse once.**
```js
   const memberGroups = new Set(
     (document.getElementById("viewerGroups")?.dataset.groups || "")
       .match(/\d+/g)?.map(Number) || [],
   );
```
3. **Gate predicate.**
```js
   const canView = (groupID) =>
     !groupID || memberGroups.has(Number(groupID)) /* + sysadmin bypass if chosen */;
```
   A group ID that is present but not a valid number must hide the item (fail closed).
4. **Apply before rendering,** not after. Skip gated items at the point where the items are built, so section counts, search, filters and "showing X of Y" stay correct with no other changes.
5. **Group field.** If items come from a form query, add the group indicator to the query's indicator map and read it like the other fields. If hardcoded, add an optional `groupID` property to each item.
6. **Empty sections.** If every item in a section is gated away, don't build that section. Make sure nothing that looks the section up later throws. If everything is gated, show the page's existing empty message.

## Rules
- Use relative paths except for other LEAF sites. No new external dependencies, no new icons, no visible UI change.
- Keep it WCAG / Section 508 accessible, responsive, and consistent with the existing code style.
- Keep comments short, only where they help a first-time reader. Remove irrelevant ones.
- Don't invent group IDs or add any to real data.
- If the file doesn't match what this prompt assumes, stop on that step, show me what the file has, and ask. Don't guess.

## Verify when done
- `node --check` on the inline script.
- Test the real functions with stubbed data (no test code left in the file):
  - No group set: visible.
  - Member of the group: visible.
  - Non-member: hidden, and counts, search and filters are correct.
  - Empty `data-groups`, missing element, or non-numeric group value: gated items hidden.
  - Every item in one section gated: the section isn't built and nothing throws.
  - Every item gated: the existing empty message shows.
- Report a short diff summary and anything you chose not to apply.

## Flag in your report
- Whether the Smarty `foreach` syntax is valid for the Smarty version in use.
- That `data-groups` must be checked in view-source on the live site, because an empty value hides every gated item, including from members.
- That viewers need read access to the group field, because unreadable means ungated and the item shows to everyone.
- That gating only hides items. The target pages must enforce their own permissions.